      "observed": "REG2.1 drives +3.3V, while the decoupling capacitors and board circuitry are on a separate +3V3 net. All VDD pins of both MCUs are explicitly unconnected rather than connected to either rail.",
      "expected": "The regulator's 3.3 V output should power the MCU VDD pins and the intended 3.3 V circuitry. The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs and sensors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\"))"
