          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU supply pins have no power connection, and the separate +3V3 net is not driven by the regulator output. The board is therefore unlikely to power or operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1", "C32", "C33", "C52", "C53"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6", "HSE1.1", "HSE1.3", "HSE2.1", "HSE2.3"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(C33-Pad1)", "Net-(C53-Pad1)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal nets connect to FCC1 pins 5 (PE6) and 37 (PE7), not its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC crystal nets have no MCU connection; NAVC1 pins 5 (PH0) and 6 (PH1) instead connect only to C37 and C38.",
      "expected": "Each 25 MHz HSE crystal circuit should connect to the corresponding MCU's HSE oscillator input and output pins. The specification identifies a 25 MHz HSE crystal for both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"90\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has the intended crystal connected to its HSE oscillator pins. The FCC crystal is routed to unrelated GPIOs, and the NAVC crystal is disconnected from the MCU, so the intended external clocking will not work.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1", "C13", "C14"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC", "unconnected-(C13-Pad1)", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)"],
      "observed": "The nets named UART3_TX_FCC and UART3_RX_FCC connect to FCC1 pins 48 and 73, both identified as VCAP, and to pins 3 and 4 of the UART3 connector. The VCAP pins are not connected to their required capacitor network; C13 has an unconnected pad and C14 is on the PH0 net.",
      "expected": "UART connector signals should use MCU UART TX/RX pins. VCAP pins should have the required local capacitor connection, not be routed as UART signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"146\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"166\") (name \"unconnected-(C13-Pad1)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"72\") (name \"Net-(FCC1-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"C14\") (pin \"1\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector exposes the MCU's VCAP nodes rather than UART signals, potentially disturbing the MCU's internal core supply and preventing UART3 communication.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the MCU supply pins are unpowered, the HSE crystals are misconnected or disconnected, and the FCC UART3 connector is routed to VCAP pins. These connectivity faults conflict with the specified powered, clocked dual-MCU design."
}

